<ul class="explain">
    <li>Arguments are shown as either <span class="inlineCodeblock">&ltarg&gt</span> or <span
            class="inlineCodeblock">[arg]</span>. Angled brackets <span class="inlineCodeblock">&ltarg&gt</span>
        are required and
        square brackets <span class="inlineCodeblock">[arg]</span> are optional.</li>
    <li>Argument values can be specified with <span class="inlineCodeblock">-key value</span> (eg. <span
            class="inlineCodeblock">-page 3</span>)</li>
    <li>Argument values with spaces (such as names) can be specified with quotes eg. <span
            class="inlineCodeblock">"saber strike"</span></li>
    <li>You can use <span class="inlineCodeblock">osuset</span> to automatically set your osu! username
        and
        gamemode for commands such as
        <span class="inlineCodeblock">recent</span> (rs)
    </li>
    <li>Mods are specified with +[mods] (include), -mx [mods] (match exact) or -me [mods] (exclude). -mx
        overrides +[mods]</li>
    <li>Gamemode can be specified by using -(mode) in commands that support it (eg. -taiko)</li>
    <li>press <a href="types.html" class="highlightLink">here</a> for an explanation on option types</li>
</ul>
